1
00:00:02,235 --> 00:00:03,503
Ten years ago.

2
00:00:04,537 --> 00:00:07,974
<i>The one who shut down</i>
<i>Michiko Daimon's father's clinic.</i>

3
00:00:12,212 --> 00:00:13,747
It wasn't me.

4
00:00:37,771 --> 00:00:40,473
DOCTOR REFERRAL AGENCY
KANBARA

5
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:47,414
<i>- Ron. </i>Seven pairs and <i>dora</i> two!
- I lost again!

6
00:00:49,149 --> 00:00:50,950
Who can it be at this hour?

7
00:00:51,117 --> 00:00:53,853
But my goodness,
you are so bad at this game.

8
00:00:53,953 --> 00:00:55,321
Anything besides surgery, right?

9
00:00:55,422 --> 00:00:56,656
Come on, Mr. Akira!

10
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,258
I'll do lots of surgeries this month...

11
00:00:58,324 --> 00:00:59,526
FREELANCE SURGEON
MICHIKO DAIMON

12
00:00:59,592 --> 00:01:02,295
- ...so lend me money.
- Michiko, watch your manners.

13
00:01:02,362 --> 00:01:03,963
- You have a visitor.
- What?

14
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:05,298
- Thank you.
- Here.

15
00:01:09,269 --> 00:01:11,137
Michiko, long time no see.

16
00:01:13,106 --> 00:01:14,841
Have you forgotten this face?

17
00:01:15,141 --> 00:01:17,444
Well, we haven't met
since you went to medical school.

18
00:01:18,344 --> 00:01:19,879
I'm the tofu shop owner.

19
00:01:21,047 --> 00:01:22,816
Mr. Musaka from the tofu shop?

20
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:26,920
- Long time, no see!
- Michiko!

21
00:01:26,986 --> 00:01:27,887
MOTOHIKO MUSAKA

22
00:01:27,954 --> 00:01:29,622
How did you know where to find me?

23
00:01:29,689 --> 00:01:33,193
When I heard you succeeded
your father and became a surgeon,

24
00:01:33,326 --> 00:01:35,562
I just had to come see you.

25
00:01:37,497 --> 00:01:40,133
Sorry for interrupting your game.
Please continue.

26
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:43,036
Are you sure?
Just one more game, so wait for me.

27
00:01:45,138 --> 00:01:47,240
I wouldn't do that if I were you.

28
00:01:47,307 --> 00:01:48,208
Really?

29
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:50,176
If you must, this one here.

30
00:01:50,243 --> 00:01:54,080
Excuse me,
but can the outsider please keep quiet?

31
00:01:54,147 --> 00:01:55,815
My apologies, I couldn't help it.

32
00:01:55,882 --> 00:01:57,016
That one, that one.

33
00:01:59,185 --> 00:02:01,754
Even then, you still do it...

34
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:03,690
<i>Ron!</i>

35
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:07,293
Look, look! <i>Kokushi musou!</i>

36
00:02:08,528 --> 00:02:10,763
Hey, what an upset win.

37
00:02:10,864 --> 00:02:12,265
She sure did us in.

38
00:02:12,332 --> 00:02:15,869
It's my first time to win
such a good hand. Thank you.

39
00:02:15,935 --> 00:02:16,936
This is nothing.

40
00:02:17,003 --> 00:02:19,939
Thanks to Michiko's father,
I'm still alive.

41
00:02:20,006 --> 00:02:21,141
- What?
- So,

42
00:02:21,207 --> 00:02:25,111
then were you a patient
at the old Daimon Clinic?

43
00:02:25,178 --> 00:02:29,549
Yes. Michiko's father operated
on my liver cancer ten years ago

44
00:02:29,616 --> 00:02:30,817
and saved my life.

45
00:02:31,784 --> 00:02:34,254
But shortly after that, he passed away.

46
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:38,925
I wanted to say thank you to Michiko
for the care her father gave me.

47
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,329
- Thank you. Bye, then.
- Are you leaving already?

48
00:02:43,396 --> 00:02:46,032
I got to see you. I'm satisfied.

49
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:48,568
- Take care, then.
- Wait.

50
00:02:50,036 --> 00:02:51,404
Mr. Musaka, are you all right?

51
00:02:51,471 --> 00:02:53,606
I just got a little dizzy, I'm fine.

52
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:54,974
- Are you sure?
- Yes. Thanks.

53
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,650
Please, it's nothing!

54
00:03:04,083 --> 00:03:05,518
How can this be nothing?

55
00:03:05,618 --> 00:03:07,387
- This is Mr. Musaka's, isn't it?
- No, no.

56
00:03:13,893 --> 00:03:16,429
Don't worry. They may not look it,
but they're all doctors.

57
00:03:17,063 --> 00:03:17,897
Doctors?

58
00:03:18,164 --> 00:03:22,202
Y-GTP 250. Bilirubin level 3.0.

59
00:03:23,403 --> 00:03:25,572
Liver function numbers are extremely bad.

60
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:27,173
Porta hepatitis.

61
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,975
What's your diagnosis, Akira?

62
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:31,644
A 6 centimeter tumor
on the bile duct at porta hepatitis.

63
00:03:32,145 --> 00:03:35,815
It's possible the liver cancer
from ten years ago metastasized.

64
00:03:36,449 --> 00:03:40,520
But a cure is possible
if he gets surgery immediately.

65
00:03:45,825 --> 00:03:49,796
What? He favors Tanaka, I don't think
he'll switch sides so easily.

66
00:03:49,862 --> 00:03:51,931
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
RYUNOSUKE BUSUJIMA

67
00:03:51,998 --> 00:03:54,968
Anyway, please handle
this matter with discretion.

68
00:03:55,034 --> 00:03:56,869
OFFICE MANAGER
KANEKO TERAYAMA

69
00:03:57,604 --> 00:03:59,339
We'll talk again later.

70
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:00,440
TAKASHI TORII

71
00:04:00,506 --> 00:04:02,108
Professor Busujima, you called?

72
00:04:02,175 --> 00:04:05,578
I have to be
at the main hospital for a while.

73
00:04:06,212 --> 00:04:08,715
I'm appointing you as the acting director.

74
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:13,486
The director and professor's race
at the main hospital is coming up,

75
00:04:13,553 --> 00:04:15,955
so Professor Busujima's very busy.

76
00:04:16,789 --> 00:04:18,925
I'm appointed the acting director...

77
00:04:20,126 --> 00:04:21,828
I will do my utmost best.

78
00:04:23,096 --> 00:04:25,865
The car from the main hospital
is here to pick you up.

79
00:04:25,965 --> 00:04:26,833
All right.

80
00:04:28,268 --> 00:04:29,936
I'm counting on you, then.

81
00:04:30,536 --> 00:04:32,805
Yes, sir.

82
00:04:36,976 --> 00:04:38,077
Good luck, sir.

83
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,795
This is Professor Torii's office.

84
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:58,164
<i>Hello. Ms. Okumura?</i>

85
00:04:58,598 --> 00:05:00,733
Professor? Did something happen?

86
00:05:01,167 --> 00:05:03,303
Where do you think I'm calling from?

87
00:05:04,103 --> 00:05:05,938
What! From the director's desk?

88
00:05:06,005 --> 00:05:07,173
SECRETARY
AI OKUMURA

89
00:05:07,573 --> 00:05:08,608
Fantastic.

90
00:05:10,777 --> 00:05:12,345
It's time for the director's rounds.

91
00:05:12,845 --> 00:05:14,247
"Director's rounds."

92
00:05:14,714 --> 00:05:15,782
Talk to you later.

93
00:05:35,568 --> 00:05:39,872
<i>Professor Torii will now start</i>
<i>his acting director rounds.</i>

94
00:05:39,939 --> 00:05:41,341
HIKARU MORIMOTO
MAMORU HARA - HIDEKI KAJI

95
00:05:41,407 --> 00:05:42,542
Acting director's rounds?

96
00:05:42,608 --> 00:05:46,212
- Does that mean he's the next director?
- It's not that simple.

97
00:05:46,446 --> 00:05:49,048
Someone may be coming
from the main hospital.

98
00:05:49,782 --> 00:05:52,218
Besides, professor's research...

99
00:05:52,752 --> 00:05:54,754
hasn't been going too well lately.

100
00:05:55,555 --> 00:05:57,757
Please take care of us.

101
00:06:09,936 --> 00:06:11,504
Professor Torii.

102
00:06:11,571 --> 00:06:13,539
You should stick out
your chest a little bit more.

103
00:06:13,606 --> 00:06:15,541
You'll appear more dignified that way.

104
00:06:17,076 --> 00:06:18,044
Very nice.

105
00:06:19,479 --> 00:06:20,813
Excuse me, I'm sorry.

106
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:24,117
- He's acting like the director--
- What?

107
00:06:24,283 --> 00:06:26,919
He's acting like the director already,
is he going to be okay?

108
00:06:30,022 --> 00:06:33,493
Look, even his secretary is here.

109
00:06:34,193 --> 00:06:36,896
He probably called her
to show her his moment of triumph.

110
00:06:50,176 --> 00:06:51,244
What is it, Dr. Daimon?

111
00:06:51,310 --> 00:06:53,579
There's a patient who needs
to be admitted immediately.

112
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:55,782
That should be discussed
with the office manager.

113
00:06:56,349 --> 00:06:59,352
I'm busy with the director's rounds.
Get out of my way.

114
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:07,126
Office Manager, please.

115
00:07:07,193 --> 00:07:09,695
All the beds in the hospital
are occupied now.

116
00:07:09,796 --> 00:07:11,798
You always have a spare room, don't you?

117
00:07:11,864 --> 00:07:12,965
That's out of the question.

118
00:07:13,032 --> 00:07:16,269
That's for emergency VIP patients.
Ordinary patients can't use it.

119
00:07:16,335 --> 00:07:19,439
Anyway, I'm begging you. If we don't
operate right away, it'll be too late.

120
00:07:19,505 --> 00:07:22,275
Anyway, the answer is no.
You'll have to look elsewhere.

121
00:07:22,341 --> 00:07:23,176
I agree.

122
00:07:28,247 --> 00:07:31,818
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

123
00:07:33,252 --> 00:07:36,389
<i>University hospital</i>
<i>medical offices were losing power</i>

124
00:07:36,856 --> 00:07:39,025
<i>and even medicine,</i>
<i>dealing with life and death,</i>

125
00:07:39,091 --> 00:07:42,261
<i>plunged into an era</i>
<i>where the law of the jungle prevailed.</i>

126
00:07:47,033 --> 00:07:48,901
- Recovery is progressing very well.
- That's great news.

127
00:07:49,902 --> 00:07:50,770
Please.

128
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:53,306
He's scheduled
to be discharged next Tuesday.

129
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:54,607
I can't.

130
00:07:55,441 --> 00:07:59,712
<i>To fill the critical shortage</i>
<i>in the medical field are the freelance.</i>

131
00:08:00,446 --> 00:08:03,883
<i>In other words, a lone wolf doctor.</i>

132
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:06,853
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

133
00:08:07,753 --> 00:08:12,358
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

134
00:08:13,626 --> 00:08:17,763
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

135
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:21,634
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

136
00:08:22,535 --> 00:08:23,603
<i>Also known as...</i>

137
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:28,508
<i>Doctor X.</i>

138
00:08:35,815 --> 00:08:38,718
DOCTOR X SURGEON MICHIKO DAIMON
EPISODE 6

139
00:08:43,656 --> 00:08:44,524
Yes.

140
00:08:44,991 --> 00:08:46,325
Director Busujima.

141
00:08:47,026 --> 00:08:50,630
Do you remember a patient
by the name of Motohiko Musaka?

142
00:08:51,097 --> 00:08:53,199
Musaka? I'm not sure.

143
00:08:53,666 --> 00:08:56,335
The patient you left to die ten years ago.

144
00:08:57,169 --> 00:09:00,172
<i>He was refused hospitalization</i>
<i>and surgery by you...</i>

145
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:02,441
<i>the Surgery Chief at the time,</i>

146
00:09:03,242 --> 00:09:07,113
and ended up getting surgery
at Daimon Clinic.

147
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:11,617
As a result, he lived
in good health for ten years,

148
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:15,922
but one month ago,
a tumor was found in the porta hepatis.

149
00:09:16,389 --> 00:09:18,024
That's unfortunate.

150
00:09:18,491 --> 00:09:21,761
So? What do you want me to do?

151
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:27,066
Surely, you won't leave Mr. Musaka
to die a second time, will you?

152
00:09:39,278 --> 00:09:41,547
Mr. Musaka, this way please.

153
00:09:42,014 --> 00:09:43,849
What a splendid room.

154
00:09:43,916 --> 00:09:45,585
Please come in.

155
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,924
You should've told me
that he's Director's special patient.

156
00:09:52,024 --> 00:09:53,993
Seriously, you are so dense.

157
00:09:54,393 --> 00:09:59,699
If there's anything you need,
please don't hesitate to tell us.

158
00:09:59,765 --> 00:10:00,967
Thank you very much.

159
00:10:03,402 --> 00:10:04,904
If you'll excuse me.

160
00:10:09,542 --> 00:10:13,145
Michiko, this room is too nice for me.

161
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,248
I know I'm going to die anyway.

162
00:10:16,315 --> 00:10:18,317
We won't know that until we test you.

163
00:10:18,384 --> 00:10:21,387
I was told at every hospital
that it was inoperable.

164
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:23,589
My wife passed away three years ago,

165
00:10:24,190 --> 00:10:27,126
and I got to see you again.
I can die without any regrets.

166
00:10:27,193 --> 00:10:30,630
It's okay. Just hurry up
and get ready to go to the lab.

167
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,302
I hope the director's rounds
went well, sir.

168
00:10:36,369 --> 00:10:38,804
It's great being the director.
Look at all this stuff I got.

169
00:10:39,739 --> 00:10:43,843
I love this chocolate very much.
One box costs 10,000 yen, you know.

170
00:10:44,443 --> 00:10:46,178
- Can I open it?
- Yes, you can.

171
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,159
Morimoto, you may go now.

172
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:02,862
Share that with the medical staff.

173
00:11:02,928 --> 00:11:04,964
- Thank you.
- Thank you for your help.

174
00:11:05,031 --> 00:11:06,432
Thank you. Excuse me.

175
00:11:13,305 --> 00:11:18,210
When you were leading the procession,
you looked wonderful.

176
00:11:18,878 --> 00:11:21,847
I wish Director Busujima
didn't have to come back.

177
00:11:21,914 --> 00:11:22,982
Hey, now.

178
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:26,252
That's okay, I'll get it.

179
00:11:29,622 --> 00:11:30,489
Hello.

180
00:11:31,757 --> 00:11:34,393
Oh, yes, this is Torii speaking.

181
00:11:35,494 --> 00:11:36,829
Yes, that's right.

182
00:11:38,597 --> 00:11:39,532
What?

183
00:11:41,434 --> 00:11:44,336
My article? What?

184
00:11:46,005 --> 00:11:50,109
Oh, thank you so much!

185
00:11:52,511 --> 00:11:53,379
Thank you.

186
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:58,117
- I did it. I finally did it.
- Professor?

187
00:11:58,184 --> 00:12:00,619
That was the international
conference selection committee.

188
00:12:00,686 --> 00:12:02,521
My research paper was selected.

189
00:12:03,355 --> 00:12:04,857
I'll get to present it in Paris.

190
00:12:05,591 --> 00:12:07,093
Congratulations!

191
00:12:07,860 --> 00:12:10,029
Luck is finally coming my way.

192
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:11,764
Professor!

193
00:12:17,770 --> 00:12:19,605
I'll check on that immediately.

194
00:12:22,341 --> 00:12:24,977
It's about Mr. Musaka
who was admitted to the special room.

195
00:12:25,044 --> 00:12:27,780
What is it suddenly?
You should at least knock.

196
00:12:27,847 --> 00:12:31,183
I'd like to operate on him immediately.
Please schedule him for surgery.

197
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:33,052
- The patient you mentioned this morning?
- Yes.

198
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,622
If he's your patient,
I'll leave it to you. Do as you please.

199
00:12:38,557 --> 00:12:39,425
Thank you...

200
00:12:40,126 --> 00:12:41,093
Professor Torii.

201
00:12:41,227 --> 00:12:43,195
I have the results
of the re-test from the other day.

202
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:45,097
I'll take a look later.

203
00:12:45,664 --> 00:12:46,632
But... Well...

204
00:12:46,699 --> 00:12:48,834
It's going to get busy!

205
00:12:53,639 --> 00:12:54,673
Well, then, excuse me.

206
00:13:16,362 --> 00:13:19,365
It won't take long. Please stay still.

207
00:13:19,865 --> 00:13:21,133
Attention, everyone.

208
00:13:22,735 --> 00:13:26,572
My "K-RAS Genetic Mutation" was selected
from among countless research papers.

209
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:30,309
I'll be presenting it
at the international conference in Paris.

210
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:31,343
What?

211
00:13:31,443 --> 00:13:34,647
- Professor, you did it!
- Congratulations!

212
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:36,816
Thank you.

213
00:13:37,583 --> 00:13:41,487
However, we can't let our guard down yet.
The conference is only a month away.

214
00:13:41,554 --> 00:13:43,489
I'll have to devote myself
to the research paper.

215
00:13:43,556 --> 00:13:45,257
Any of you with free time,
please cooperate.

216
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:47,993
- Yes, Professor.
- We'll be happy to help you.

217
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:51,564
Professor, I wish I could help, but...

218
00:13:51,630 --> 00:13:54,300
Kaji, you're busy with surgeries, I know.

219
00:13:54,366 --> 00:13:57,169
- The rest of you, please help.
- Will do.

220
00:13:58,103 --> 00:13:59,805
I'm not doing it.

221
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:05,277
I know that.
But you'll regret not helping.

222
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:08,581
This will be a historical presentation
that may open

223
00:14:08,781 --> 00:14:10,616
a new door to genetic medicine.

224
00:14:11,617 --> 00:14:12,751
Talk to you later.

225
00:14:21,827 --> 00:14:23,762
He's on top of the world.

226
00:14:23,829 --> 00:14:26,365
If he succeeds, forget about
the director of a satellite hospital,

227
00:14:26,432 --> 00:14:29,201
he might get a big promotion
to the main hospital.

228
00:14:29,268 --> 00:14:31,170
I don't know, he's pretty meek.

229
00:14:31,337 --> 00:14:33,672
I bet he's taking
his mistress to Paris, too.

230
00:14:33,739 --> 00:14:35,574
What? Mistress?

231
00:14:35,641 --> 00:14:37,409
I don't know how
he keeps it from his wife.

232
00:14:37,476 --> 00:14:38,878
I'm sure she knows.

233
00:14:38,944 --> 00:14:41,947
Right about now,
I bet his wife's gathering evidence

234
00:14:42,014 --> 00:14:43,749
to take him to the cleaners
after the divorce.

235
00:14:43,816 --> 00:14:47,319
It sounds real coming from you
who's gone through a divorce.

236
00:14:48,587 --> 00:14:51,557
Wait. Who's this mistress?

237
00:14:52,024 --> 00:14:54,526
You moron! The whole hospital knows.

238
00:14:56,962 --> 00:14:59,498
What? Do you know, too?

239
00:14:59,598 --> 00:15:00,866
- Of course.
- What!

240
00:15:01,834 --> 00:15:03,068
Who's this mistress?

241
00:15:03,836 --> 00:15:06,272
Oh, it's time to collect blood.

242
00:15:08,474 --> 00:15:09,441
Dr. Daimon--

243
00:15:11,010 --> 00:15:13,846
You're not interested
in something like this, are you?

244
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,214
Nope.

245
00:15:16,048 --> 00:15:17,216
But I know.

246
00:15:17,549 --> 00:15:21,520
- What! How come even you know it?
- They were embracing earlier.

247
00:15:22,521 --> 00:15:24,857
- Gross!
- Oh, no.

248
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:27,159
Who was it?
I'm a member of the medical staff, too.

249
00:15:27,259 --> 00:15:29,295
- Please tell me!
- You're annoying.

250
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:32,097
Why don't you go help out
with the research paper?

251
00:15:32,231 --> 00:15:33,198
Morimoto,

252
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:34,166
let's go!

253
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:36,268
Yes!

254
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:40,339
Are you eyeing
the gratuity from a VIP again?

255
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:44,877
Who's this Mr. Musaka in the special room?

256
00:15:45,210 --> 00:15:48,347
- A tycoon? Investor?
- Owner of a tofu shop.

257
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:50,049
Surely, you jest.

258
00:15:54,653 --> 00:15:57,656
If it permeates the hepatic artery,
it could be bad.

259
00:15:58,457 --> 00:15:59,491
We have to hurry.

260
00:16:11,603 --> 00:16:13,639
- Yes.
- This is Shiraki from Radiation.

261
00:16:13,706 --> 00:16:16,075
Have you had a chance
to look at the test results?

262
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:19,378
Oh, that. No, I've been too busy,
I forgot about it.

263
00:16:19,712 --> 00:16:23,515
<i>Look at it right away,</i>
<i>and get a CT scan immediately, please.</i>

264
00:16:25,918 --> 00:16:27,019
Please.

265
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,128
I'm back.

266
00:17:09,828 --> 00:17:15,134
For your late-night snack,
I bought you Stamina Moo Moo Bento.

267
00:17:17,736 --> 00:17:19,605
And to keep the tea hot...

268
00:17:21,573 --> 00:17:22,474
I kept it here.

269
00:17:23,575 --> 00:17:24,910
- Here.
- Thanks.

270
00:17:25,778 --> 00:17:27,446
You can leave now for today.

271
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:29,248
Yes.

272
00:17:30,582 --> 00:17:32,818
It got cold suddenly, didn't it?

273
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:35,888
It must be even colder in Paris.

274
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:39,591
I'll have to buy a new coat.

275
00:17:41,927 --> 00:17:42,895
Ms. Okumura.

276
00:17:45,964 --> 00:17:47,433
I'll buy you a new coat.

277
00:17:48,967 --> 00:17:49,968
I can't wait.

278
00:17:50,469 --> 00:17:51,403
But...

279
00:17:52,671 --> 00:17:53,539
What is it?

280
00:17:54,006 --> 00:17:56,442
I may not be able to go to Paris.

281
00:17:57,242 --> 00:17:58,177
What?

282
00:18:00,612 --> 00:18:02,347
What are you talking about?

283
00:18:02,981 --> 00:18:04,249
Don't worry!

284
00:18:04,450 --> 00:18:07,519
I'm sure you can finish
your research paper.

285
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:12,958
Build up your stamina, and hang in there.

286
00:18:13,992 --> 00:18:14,993
Moo moo.

287
00:18:32,344 --> 00:18:35,247
CA19-9 is 135.

288
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:38,884
CEA, 25.

289
00:18:41,653 --> 00:18:42,621
It can't be.

290
00:18:44,389 --> 00:18:45,290
Malignant?

291
00:18:51,730 --> 00:18:53,098
HOME

292
00:18:57,336 --> 00:18:58,370
Hello.

293
00:18:59,771 --> 00:19:01,940
Yeah, I'll be late again tonight.

294
00:19:03,408 --> 00:19:06,845
What? Kentaro's grades went down again?

295
00:19:08,113 --> 00:19:10,849
No, I still have work to do today.

296
00:19:11,483 --> 00:19:13,352
All right, you can tell me tomorrow.

297
00:19:16,288 --> 00:19:18,524
I told you I'm working! Knock it off!

298
00:19:38,143 --> 00:19:39,178
This is...

299
00:19:46,685 --> 00:19:48,253
Hilar bile duct cancer.

300
00:19:48,687 --> 00:19:50,856
The tumor is approximately 3 centimeters.

301
00:19:52,224 --> 00:19:53,792
I'd say it is Stage 2.

302
00:19:59,765 --> 00:20:00,966
Is it more advanced?

303
00:20:10,242 --> 00:20:13,312
I can't believe this.
I don't even have any symptoms.

304
00:20:14,012 --> 00:20:16,615
You're always telling
your patients yourself

305
00:20:16,682 --> 00:20:18,917
that liver and bile ducts
are silent organs.

306
00:20:21,486 --> 00:20:22,988
Surgery is needed as soon as possible.

307
00:20:23,989 --> 00:20:26,458
You've got to be kidding.
Not at an important time like this.

308
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:27,392
Professor.

309
00:20:29,928 --> 00:20:30,796
Shiraki.

310
00:20:31,597 --> 00:20:34,433
Don't tell anyone about this.

311
00:20:38,370 --> 00:20:39,238
Please.

312
00:20:45,611 --> 00:20:47,879
We will now begin
this week's pre-surgery conference.

313
00:20:47,946 --> 00:20:50,716
First case. Motohiko Musaka, 62 years old.

314
00:20:50,782 --> 00:20:51,950
PRE-OPERATION CONFERENCE

315
00:20:52,818 --> 00:20:55,621
Ten years ago, he had surgery
to remove liver cancer.

316
00:20:55,687 --> 00:20:57,189
There was no relapse,

317
00:20:57,256 --> 00:21:01,093
but one month ago, a tumor was found
in the area of porta hepatis.

318
00:21:01,159 --> 00:21:04,730
Test results confirmed
a 6 centimeter tumor.

319
00:21:04,830 --> 00:21:08,267
Pre-surgery diagnosis
is Stage 3 hilar bile duct cancer.

320
00:21:08,967 --> 00:21:10,969
From the image,
preservation of the portal vein is...

321
00:21:12,838 --> 00:21:14,473
<i>Hilar bile duct cancer.</i>

322
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:17,609
It's believed there's
quite a bit of adhesion as well.

323
00:21:18,343 --> 00:21:19,344
Professor Torii?

324
00:21:20,579 --> 00:21:21,546
Professor Torii?

325
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:24,816
Have you decided on the primary surgeon?

326
00:21:25,183 --> 00:21:27,286
- What?
- I'll be the primary surgeon.

327
00:21:28,654 --> 00:21:30,455
I have the professor's permission already.

328
00:21:30,522 --> 00:21:31,590
Wait a minute.

329
00:21:34,059 --> 00:21:36,128
Resection of hilar bile duct cancer

330
00:21:36,261 --> 00:21:38,563
is dangerous unless it's done
by an experienced surgeon.

331
00:21:39,831 --> 00:21:41,767
Professor, I'll perform the surgery.

332
00:21:42,234 --> 00:21:45,504
This patient is
the Director's special patient.

333
00:21:45,604 --> 00:21:48,106
There will be trouble
if anything happens to him.

334
00:21:48,173 --> 00:21:52,911
I think we should go with Dr. Kaji,
who has a lot of experience.

335
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:54,212
Yes, you're right.

336
00:21:54,546 --> 00:21:55,847
Let's have Kaji do it.

337
00:21:56,248 --> 00:21:58,917
Why? That's not what you told me.

338
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:01,486
You said you'd leave it to me, didn't you?

339
00:22:01,553 --> 00:22:03,655
- Yes. But, Daimon--
- What is this?

340
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:07,626
Oh, no. This is not good...

341
00:22:10,062 --> 00:22:11,463
Even I can't cut this.

342
00:22:12,731 --> 00:22:14,800
- What?
- Preoperative diagnosis

343
00:22:14,866 --> 00:22:17,302
is extremely difficult
for hilar bile duct cancer.

344
00:22:17,369 --> 00:22:18,937
Speaking from my experience...

345
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:22,607
this is impossible to remove.

346
00:22:23,642 --> 00:22:24,609
Impossible to remove?

347
00:22:28,980 --> 00:22:30,716
Even Dr. Kaji can't do it?

348
00:22:31,717 --> 00:22:33,719
Hilar bile duct cancer
is the most difficult surgery

349
00:22:33,785 --> 00:22:35,320
among gastrointestinal cancer.

350
00:22:35,487 --> 00:22:38,557
You have to cut into the porta hepatis
area where the bile duct, portal vein,

351
00:22:38,623 --> 00:22:40,492
and hepatic artery intricately intersect.

352
00:22:42,661 --> 00:22:46,064
In this patient's case,
it's too far advanced in the area.

353
00:22:47,265 --> 00:22:50,435
Liver function is poor
and his general condition is not good.

354
00:22:51,269 --> 00:22:54,806
The only thing we can do is
not do the surgery and prolong his life.

355
00:22:56,241 --> 00:22:58,477
Why can't you operate on him?
It can be done.

356
00:22:59,878 --> 00:23:01,913
Daimon, can you do it?

357
00:23:02,781 --> 00:23:04,850
Yes. I can do it.

358
00:23:05,550 --> 00:23:07,419
- Are you serious?
- I'm serious.

359
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:09,488
It's a major surgery
lasting more than 12 hours

360
00:23:09,554 --> 00:23:12,991
involving hepatectomy, bile duct
excision, and lymph node dissection.

361
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:14,459
The patient can't endure it.

362
00:23:14,993 --> 00:23:16,795
He'll bleed to death during surgery.

363
00:23:24,603 --> 00:23:25,437
Hey.

364
00:23:26,505 --> 00:23:28,640
Why are you pretending to be asleep?

365
00:23:31,343 --> 00:23:35,480
<i>Resection of the right liver lobe,</i>
<i>the bile duct, and the caudate lobe.</i>

366
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:38,984
<i>And then detach the bile duct cancer</i>
<i>from the portal vein</i>

367
00:23:39,050 --> 00:23:41,620
<i>and hepatic artery and cut it off</i>
<i>just before it enters the liver.</i>

368
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:44,589
<i>After that, connect</i>
<i>the intrahepatic bile duct.</i>

369
00:23:50,796 --> 00:23:55,300
It may take Dr. Kaji twelve hours,
but I can do it in six.

370
00:23:56,134 --> 00:23:57,102
What?

371
00:23:57,169 --> 00:23:58,537
I'm fast.

372
00:23:58,904 --> 00:24:00,772
And I don't make mistakes.

373
00:24:01,573 --> 00:24:03,809
The high regard you have
for yourself is abnormal.

374
00:24:04,409 --> 00:24:05,544
This patient's going to die.

375
00:24:05,811 --> 00:24:09,481
- If we don't do anything, he'll die.
- No, he'll die if you operate on him.

376
00:24:09,548 --> 00:24:12,184
- I'll save him by operating on him.
- Resection is impossible.

377
00:24:12,250 --> 00:24:13,852
No, it's not impossible.

378
00:24:14,719 --> 00:24:17,589
Professor, please talk to her.

379
00:24:22,527 --> 00:24:24,429
Daimon, is it really possible?

380
00:24:25,030 --> 00:24:25,864
Yes.

381
00:24:26,331 --> 00:24:27,265
And you won't fail either?

382
00:24:28,099 --> 00:24:29,134
Yes.

383
00:24:31,603 --> 00:24:32,804
Perform the surgery.

384
00:24:34,539 --> 00:24:35,740
Professor.

385
00:24:37,142 --> 00:24:38,543
You can leave it to me.

386
00:24:40,045 --> 00:24:41,046
You can't be serious.

387
00:24:49,921 --> 00:24:51,857
Professor's usually so cautious.

388
00:24:52,858 --> 00:24:54,192
What happened to him today?

389
00:24:54,259 --> 00:24:56,695
Then the primary surgeon for this surgery

390
00:24:56,761 --> 00:24:58,997
will be Dr. Daimon.

391
00:24:59,865 --> 00:25:02,634
Continuing on with the next case...

392
00:25:09,207 --> 00:25:12,477
Mr. Musaka, the date
of your surgery has been decided.

393
00:25:13,245 --> 00:25:14,246
What?

394
00:25:14,713 --> 00:25:17,649
The day after tomorrow.
Dr. Daimon is your primary surgeon.

395
00:25:17,716 --> 00:25:20,418
I'm Morimoto, her assistant.
Pleased to meet you.

396
00:25:22,420 --> 00:25:25,624
Michiko. Are you going
to perform surgery on me?

397
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:26,691
Michiko?

398
00:25:26,758 --> 00:25:30,729
All the hospitals I went to said it was
inoperable and they gave up on me.

399
00:25:31,096 --> 00:25:34,533
But can you really perform surgery
on my cancer?

400
00:25:34,599 --> 00:25:35,634
Yes.

401
00:25:36,368 --> 00:25:38,670
I don't make mistakes.

402
00:25:42,641 --> 00:25:46,211
Does that mean I can live?

403
00:26:00,158 --> 00:26:01,192
Truly.

404
00:26:02,861 --> 00:26:05,630
Michiko, you're
Dr. Daimon's daughter after all.

405
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:10,502
Thank you.

406
00:26:13,004 --> 00:26:14,673
I'm counting on you.

407
00:26:17,375 --> 00:26:18,376
Come on.

408
00:26:19,811 --> 00:26:20,812
Thank you.

409
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:33,592
Dr. Daimon, is your father a surgeon, too?

410
00:26:33,792 --> 00:26:36,294
I don't engage in that kind of small talk.

411
00:26:36,795 --> 00:26:40,165
Let me change the question, then.
Did you used to be called Michiko?

412
00:26:40,332 --> 00:26:41,900
That's cute.

413
00:26:41,967 --> 00:26:45,537
Then from now on, is it okay
if I call you Dr. Michiko?

414
00:26:58,483 --> 00:27:01,019
Hey, let me see the images again.

415
00:27:05,190 --> 00:27:06,558
Are these Mr. Musaka's?

416
00:27:06,958 --> 00:27:09,861
Yes, they are.
Let me show you more detailed ones.

417
00:27:14,599 --> 00:27:16,901
Yes, these are Mr. Musaka's. Wait...

418
00:27:17,569 --> 00:27:18,536
Then whose were those?

419
00:27:20,739 --> 00:27:22,574
They're not Mr. Musaka's, are they?

420
00:27:24,009 --> 00:27:24,909
Does that mean

421
00:27:25,010 --> 00:27:27,679
there's another patient with
a severe case of hilar bile duct cancer?

422
00:27:27,746 --> 00:27:30,115
No, there isn't.
I told you, they're Mr. Musaka's.

423
00:27:39,924 --> 00:27:41,926
MOTOHIKO MUSAKA

424
00:27:45,430 --> 00:27:47,565
Those are definitely someone else's.

425
00:27:48,366 --> 00:27:51,236
If it's not a patient...

426
00:27:54,039 --> 00:27:55,940
What are you mumbling about?

427
00:27:58,109 --> 00:27:59,010
Michiko,

428
00:27:59,744 --> 00:28:01,980
you're operating
on Mr. Musaka, aren't you?

429
00:28:02,647 --> 00:28:06,351
I've done that surgery, too,
but it's a tough one.

430
00:28:06,618 --> 00:28:10,355
On your feet for more than ten hours
without eating or drinking.

431
00:28:11,589 --> 00:28:12,557
You can't even pee--

432
00:28:12,657 --> 00:28:15,860
There's one more person
I have to operate on.

433
00:28:16,561 --> 00:28:17,395
What?

434
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:29,207
Professor, you don't look well.

435
00:28:30,642 --> 00:28:32,410
Are you working too hard on your paper?

436
00:28:32,977 --> 00:28:35,747
If you push yourself too hard,
you'll make yourself ill.

437
00:28:35,847 --> 00:28:37,215
You have to unwind once in a while.

438
00:28:37,916 --> 00:28:41,486
You're right. How about
living it up at Ginza tonight, huh?

439
00:28:44,155 --> 00:28:48,426
Professor Torii, this is terrible!
I just heard an unbelievable rumor!

440
00:28:49,227 --> 00:28:52,964
Busujima... Director Busujima is trying
to bring Professor Hijikata

441
00:28:53,031 --> 00:28:55,467
from the main hospital
to this Surgery Department II.

442
00:28:56,468 --> 00:28:58,436
- What?
- Please come with me.

443
00:28:59,237 --> 00:29:01,473
Run!

444
00:29:04,008 --> 00:29:06,778
Hijikata's that guy who became
a professor at the age of 38

445
00:29:06,845 --> 00:29:09,848
at Chicago Medical University
and returned home in triumph.

446
00:29:10,148 --> 00:29:11,316
Is that true?

447
00:29:11,382 --> 00:29:13,885
He's the star of Teito Medical University.

448
00:29:13,952 --> 00:29:17,889
<i>Professor Hijikata's coming</i>
<i>to Surgery Department II?</i>

449
00:29:18,356 --> 00:29:20,959
<i>What the heck is</i>
<i>Director Busujima thinking?</i>

450
00:29:24,696 --> 00:29:27,632
Torii must've heard by now that

451
00:29:28,299 --> 00:29:31,169
Hijikata's coming to the Third Hospital.

452
00:29:32,170 --> 00:29:34,038
Isn't that a good thing?

453
00:29:35,006 --> 00:29:38,109
It would be
a good stimulus for Torii, too.

454
00:29:38,977 --> 00:29:43,148
Let's have him work hard
for the international conference.

455
00:29:44,382 --> 00:29:48,052
Research and papers are
the only things he's got going for him.

456
00:29:49,621 --> 00:29:54,592
He sure doesn't have
a knack for surgery or politics.

457
00:29:56,861 --> 00:29:59,397
<i>And what are you planning to do?</i>

458
00:29:59,464 --> 00:30:04,035
<i>I think it's best to have him</i>
<i>have a friendly competition with Hijikata.</i>

459
00:30:06,437 --> 00:30:07,772
If he doesn't make it,

460
00:30:08,439 --> 00:30:11,509
there are other satellite hospitals
in the rural area where business is slow.

461
00:30:12,043 --> 00:30:15,980
He can take it easy
and do his research there.

462
00:30:19,050 --> 00:30:21,719
<i>He more or less destroyed</i>
<i>Daimon Clinic, didn't he?</i>

463
00:30:22,187 --> 00:30:23,188
I guess.

464
00:30:23,488 --> 00:30:26,558
He rejected all patients
who were referred by Daimon Clinic,

465
00:30:26,658 --> 00:30:30,695
and wouldn't allow them
to be hospitalized or have surgery.

466
00:30:31,029 --> 00:30:35,834
A private practitioner cut off
by university hospital is pathetic.

467
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:39,804
What made him turn against
the clinic to that extreme?

468
00:30:40,438 --> 00:30:43,942
When Busujima was
running for Surgery Chief,

469
00:30:44,008 --> 00:30:46,010
you know, he needed money, right?

470
00:30:46,077 --> 00:30:48,279
He raised funds from all over the place,

471
00:30:48,413 --> 00:30:51,783
and he approached Daimon Clinic,
who was his classmate.

472
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:54,853
However, Dr. Daimon refused.

473
00:30:54,919 --> 00:30:59,123
Because he saw through
Busujima's character as a surgeon.

474
00:31:00,325 --> 00:31:03,828
Busujima became the Surgery Chief,
bore a grudge against him for that,

475
00:31:03,895 --> 00:31:07,031
<i>and he put pressure</i>
<i>on other affiliated hospitals as well.</i>

476
00:31:08,566 --> 00:31:11,269
He's the worst, that Busujima.

477
00:31:11,769 --> 00:31:13,805
Akira, how do you know all this?

478
00:31:14,405 --> 00:31:18,276
We were classmates at medical school.

479
00:31:18,743 --> 00:31:20,144
- What!
- What?

480
00:31:20,578 --> 00:31:21,613
<i>Riichi.</i>

481
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:22,814
What?

482
00:31:23,081 --> 00:31:26,918
Wait. You were classmates
with Michiko's father and Busujima, too?

483
00:31:26,985 --> 00:31:30,722
Busujima loved power since he was
a member of the medical staff.

484
00:31:30,955 --> 00:31:32,523
I love money very much.

485
00:31:32,924 --> 00:31:36,394
Hiroshi Daimon was
the only genuine doctor.

486
00:31:36,961 --> 00:31:40,331
Saddled with the clinic's debt,
Michiko had it tough, too.

487
00:31:40,765 --> 00:31:45,069
That's why I took over her debt for her.

488
00:31:45,536 --> 00:31:47,171
That's it.

489
00:31:47,639 --> 00:31:48,773
<i>Ron.</i>

490
00:31:50,375 --> 00:31:52,977
<i>Mentan Pin Sanshoku.</i>

491
00:31:53,645 --> 00:31:54,812
<i>Dora dora.</i>

492
00:31:55,713 --> 00:31:56,648
<i>Baiman.</i>

493
00:31:56,714 --> 00:32:01,786
So, why did Mr. Akira quit surgery?

494
00:32:02,253 --> 00:32:03,755
That's a secret.

495
00:32:17,435 --> 00:32:19,904
Dr. Morimoto,
Mr. Musaka in the special room...

496
00:32:20,238 --> 00:32:21,205
Doctor!

497
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:33,818
Mr. Musaka, are you all right? Mr. Musaka!

498
00:32:33,885 --> 00:32:37,121
Mr. Musaka, are you all right?
Excuse me, I'm opening your gown.

499
00:32:47,098 --> 00:32:49,233
- Hello.
- Dr. Daimon, please come right away.

500
00:32:49,300 --> 00:32:51,069
Mr. Musaka's condition took a sudden turn.

501
00:32:51,135 --> 00:32:53,237
<i>He has impaired consciousness.</i>
<i>His hands are trembling.</i>

502
00:33:05,016 --> 00:33:07,385
Michiko, what's the matter?
You look so serious.

503
00:33:07,518 --> 00:33:08,619
Morimoto, what's going on?

504
00:33:09,087 --> 00:33:10,355
Well...

505
00:33:10,421 --> 00:33:12,590
Didn't you say
his consciousness was fading?

506
00:33:12,657 --> 00:33:14,459
It was for a while, but...

507
00:33:14,525 --> 00:33:17,295
Michiko, that's the truth.
When Dr. Morimoto came,

508
00:33:17,362 --> 00:33:19,063
I felt relieved and it went away.

509
00:33:19,163 --> 00:33:21,199
- Be quiet for a minute.
- But it's true.

510
00:33:21,265 --> 00:33:25,303
So, since you're here anyway,
let's have some fun.

511
00:33:27,105 --> 00:33:28,940
- I'll go pour some tea!
- Thanks.

512
00:33:32,443 --> 00:33:33,578
All right.

513
00:33:34,746 --> 00:33:37,348
You had surgery done at a clinic?

514
00:33:37,448 --> 00:33:39,517
Yes. I don't know why,

515
00:33:39,584 --> 00:33:42,086
but I couldn't get treatment
at the university hospital.

516
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:46,758
Dr. Daimon himself took the scalpel
and removed the cancer.

517
00:33:47,392 --> 00:33:49,360
And this time, his daughter, Michiko.

518
00:33:49,560 --> 00:33:52,530
Dr. Michiko fought hard for you
at the conference, too.

519
00:33:52,597 --> 00:33:54,665
Is that right? Thank you.

520
00:33:55,500 --> 00:33:58,703
You gave me strength to live
when you said you'd operate on me.

521
00:33:59,704 --> 00:34:03,374
Even before the surgery, I feel
all better as if the cancer disappeared.

522
00:34:04,308 --> 00:34:07,745
Take it easy tomorrow
and go to sleep as early as possible.

523
00:34:08,079 --> 00:34:11,349
If you feel your consciousness
fading, call the nurse immediately.

524
00:34:11,416 --> 00:34:14,886
She's as unsociable as ever.
She took after her father.

525
00:34:15,019 --> 00:34:17,522
But she's actually really nice. Yes.

526
00:34:19,724 --> 00:34:21,025
Someone's coming. Oh, no.

527
00:34:28,132 --> 00:34:29,200
Mr. Musaka?

528
00:34:31,702 --> 00:34:32,837
Mr. Musaka?

529
00:34:36,641 --> 00:34:38,342
What are you guys doing?

530
00:34:40,511 --> 00:34:42,013
Not you, too, Dr. Daimon.

531
00:34:42,547 --> 00:34:44,148
Won't you join us, too?

532
00:34:47,718 --> 00:34:48,886
Okay, here we go.

533
00:34:54,292 --> 00:34:56,227
I can't get a match at all.

534
00:34:58,329 --> 00:35:01,199
Wait and see. I'm going
to turn things around big-time.

535
00:35:02,300 --> 00:35:05,103
I got a match!

536
00:35:37,168 --> 00:35:40,605
Dr. Daimon! Doctor! ER called.

537
00:35:40,671 --> 00:35:42,773
A patient with external injuries
on the left chest

538
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:44,675
and the abdominal area
needs emergency surgery.

539
00:35:48,045 --> 00:35:49,046
Excuse me.

540
00:35:49,580 --> 00:35:51,282
Bruising on the left lung,
damage to multiple organs

541
00:35:51,349 --> 00:35:54,519
including left kidney
and spleen. He's in hemorrhagic shock.

542
00:35:54,585 --> 00:35:57,221
Even after administering catecholamine,
blood pressure is barely 60.

543
00:36:00,391 --> 00:36:01,459
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

544
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:17,508
The left splenic artery is ruptured
and bleeding. We will repair it.

545
00:36:18,342 --> 00:36:19,610
- Lower the loupe, please.
- Yes.

546
00:36:23,114 --> 00:36:24,248
- 8-0 nylon.
- Yes.

547
00:36:46,404 --> 00:36:47,772
- Sweat.
- Yes.

548
00:36:49,140 --> 00:36:50,041
Excuse me.

549
00:36:51,709 --> 00:36:53,244
There's a crack in the spleen.

550
00:36:53,678 --> 00:36:56,581
But in this case,
pressure hemostasis should work.

551
00:36:56,914 --> 00:36:59,650
- Prepare to administer hemostatic.
- Please bring the hemostatic drug.

552
00:36:59,717 --> 00:37:00,851
- Gauze.
- Yes.

553
00:37:08,859 --> 00:37:09,860
Excuse me.

554
00:37:11,929 --> 00:37:15,233
Mr. Musaka, good morning.
How are you feeling?

555
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:18,302
Please don't tell anyone about last night.

556
00:37:19,403 --> 00:37:21,439
I'll be reprimanded.

557
00:37:21,739 --> 00:37:22,940
Please don't say anything.

558
00:37:25,776 --> 00:37:26,911
Mr. Musaka.

559
00:37:37,288 --> 00:37:40,224
The left kidney is severely damaged.

560
00:37:42,026 --> 00:37:44,962
Hemostasis is difficult.
Remove the left kidney.

561
00:37:45,029 --> 00:37:45,896
Got it.

562
00:37:48,332 --> 00:37:49,834
- Curved Kelly.
- Yes.

563
00:37:53,237 --> 00:37:54,538
How's the blood pressure?

564
00:37:55,573 --> 00:37:58,276
It's improving with transfusion.
90 over 50.

565
00:38:12,023 --> 00:38:13,491
We did everything we could, but...

566
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:57,601
I heard that patient of yours...

567
00:38:59,070 --> 00:39:01,439
was laughing in good spirits last night?

568
00:39:05,943 --> 00:39:07,078
Hey, say something.

569
00:39:09,714 --> 00:39:10,981
I'm frustrated with myself.

570
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:17,621
If I had operated on him
three days sooner, he would've survived.

571
00:39:19,890 --> 00:39:21,492
I'm frustrated with myself.

572
00:39:27,398 --> 00:39:29,900
All surgeons experience
that sort of thing.

573
00:39:31,268 --> 00:39:34,071
- You should be used to it by now.
- No, I can't get used to it.

574
00:39:36,440 --> 00:39:38,042
I'm frustrated with myself.

575
00:39:45,950 --> 00:39:47,918
I don't like sick people.

576
00:39:49,887 --> 00:39:50,721
What?

577
00:39:52,423 --> 00:39:55,426
What do you mean?
Why did you decide to be a doctor?

578
00:39:56,827 --> 00:39:59,463
I decided to be a surgeon
because I don't like sick people.

579
00:40:02,166 --> 00:40:03,434
I want to operate on them...

580
00:40:04,902 --> 00:40:06,637
and save them no matter what.

581
00:40:13,444 --> 00:40:15,045
Somewhere in this hospital,

582
00:40:15,613 --> 00:40:18,949
there's a patient
with the same cancer as Mr. Musaka.

583
00:40:19,350 --> 00:40:20,518
What?

584
00:40:21,585 --> 00:40:22,653
Wait a minute.

585
00:40:32,563 --> 00:40:35,566
Professor. I got this much ready
for your research paper.

586
00:40:46,644 --> 00:40:47,545
Director.

587
00:40:49,847 --> 00:40:52,583
Sorry for interrupting
your work on your paper.

588
00:40:53,350 --> 00:40:57,354
So, did anything happen during my absence?

589
00:40:59,790 --> 00:41:00,991
Please rest assured.

590
00:41:01,058 --> 00:41:04,595
Professor Torii did a fine job
as acting director.

591
00:41:04,662 --> 00:41:05,529
Is that right?

592
00:41:06,464 --> 00:41:08,799
- I'm glad to hear that.
- Yes, sir.

593
00:41:14,205 --> 00:41:16,040
- Director.
- What is it?

594
00:41:18,943 --> 00:41:21,912
Is it true that Hijikata's
coming to this hospital?

595
00:41:24,982 --> 00:41:25,983
Yes.

596
00:41:27,785 --> 00:41:32,156
Come to think of it, he was
once your assistant, wasn't he?

597
00:41:33,023 --> 00:41:36,794
He's young, but outstanding,
so I decided to bring him.

598
00:41:38,462 --> 00:41:39,797
So, you're bringing him here?

599
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:49,607
We don't need two professors
in Surgery Department II.

600
00:41:51,942 --> 00:41:54,578
I served the Third Hospital
to the best of my ability.

601
00:41:54,645 --> 00:41:56,280
I worked hard for this hospital,

602
00:41:56,514 --> 00:41:58,549
bringing in more patients
and training a great staff.

603
00:41:58,616 --> 00:42:00,384
In addition, my research paper

604
00:42:00,618 --> 00:42:02,253
received high praise at the conference,

605
00:42:03,587 --> 00:42:06,023
and I flatter myself that
I raised the value of the hospital.

606
00:42:06,590 --> 00:42:08,692
I know that, too.

607
00:42:09,727 --> 00:42:12,763
However, in order to increase
the number of patients further

608
00:42:13,230 --> 00:42:16,867
and for the hospital to rise in ranks
and survive in times like this,

609
00:42:16,934 --> 00:42:20,104
we also need a star like Hijikata.

610
00:42:20,170 --> 00:42:21,639
It's true my sole interest...

611
00:42:22,907 --> 00:42:25,976
lies in research and I'm not flashy.

612
00:42:26,610 --> 00:42:29,346
But a professor's value
shouldn't be determined

613
00:42:29,980 --> 00:42:32,783
by superficial things such as star quality

614
00:42:33,484 --> 00:42:35,219
and having worldly ways.

615
00:42:35,853 --> 00:42:37,288
- Torii.
- I will not...

616
00:42:37,922 --> 00:42:39,890
give up the Surgery Chief's seat.

617
00:42:40,591 --> 00:42:43,827
The international conference
is right around the corner.

618
00:42:43,994 --> 00:42:45,763
I'll achieve huge success in Paris

619
00:42:46,196 --> 00:42:49,967
and protect my Surgery Chief's position.
No matter what it takes.

620
00:42:50,834 --> 00:42:52,336
Surgery Chief's position?

621
00:42:53,037 --> 00:42:54,371
International Conference?

622
00:42:54,939 --> 00:42:57,007
Now's not the time for that.

623
00:42:57,474 --> 00:42:59,910
Ms. Daimon,
we're discussing complex matters--

624
00:43:00,044 --> 00:43:02,513
If we don't hurry, it'll be something
that cannot be undone.

625
00:43:02,980 --> 00:43:03,948
Like Mr. Musaka.

626
00:43:05,683 --> 00:43:07,217
Like Mr. Musaka?

627
00:43:07,284 --> 00:43:08,886
What are you talking about?

628
00:43:11,422 --> 00:43:13,624
Surely you're not saying
Professor Torii...

629
00:43:15,793 --> 00:43:18,462
Indeed, I have absolutely no idea
what you're talking about.

630
00:43:22,433 --> 00:43:23,500
Professor Torii...

631
00:43:25,936 --> 00:43:28,472
like Mr. Musaka...

632
00:43:29,840 --> 00:43:31,976
you have hilar bile duct cancer,
don't you?

633
00:43:32,643 --> 00:43:33,544
What?

634
00:43:37,848 --> 00:43:41,685
Your position as Surgery Chief
or your life...

635
00:43:43,320 --> 00:43:44,888
Which one are you going to choose?

636
00:43:48,058 --> 00:43:50,828
Is what she said true?

637
00:43:52,496 --> 00:43:54,231
It's just a false allegation.

638
00:43:55,132 --> 00:43:56,700
It's nothing but nonsense.

639
00:43:57,868 --> 00:44:00,471
At an important time like this,
right before the conference.

640
00:44:00,771 --> 00:44:02,473
What kind of nonsense are you bringing up?

641
00:44:05,242 --> 00:44:10,648
Even if it was true,
this is not the place to talk about it!

642
00:44:11,015 --> 00:44:12,683
You're getting yourself in trouble here!

643
00:44:13,484 --> 00:44:16,687
Director, as you can see,
I'm perfectly healthy.

644
00:44:17,488 --> 00:44:18,722
Please believe me.

645
00:44:22,026 --> 00:44:25,429
Please don't cast me aside.

646
00:44:38,575 --> 00:44:39,677
Daimon.

647
00:44:41,145 --> 00:44:45,516
You've made a cancer patient
out of Torii in front of everyone.

648
00:44:46,617 --> 00:44:47,851
What for?

649
00:44:51,488 --> 00:44:53,123
Do you want to bring him down?

650
00:44:56,627 --> 00:44:57,995
Are you stupid or what?

651
00:44:59,763 --> 00:45:02,466
It's because we don't have
a moment to spare, of course.

652
00:45:05,436 --> 00:45:06,503
Professor Torii.

653
00:45:08,872 --> 00:45:10,541
Let me operate on you.

654
00:45:14,745 --> 00:45:16,246
I will not fail.

655
00:45:30,694 --> 00:45:32,696
Subtitle translation by Kelly True

656
00:45:32,796 --> 00:45:33,630
PREVIEW

657
00:45:33,697 --> 00:45:35,766
Aren't doctors obligated
to tell the truth?

658
00:45:36,100 --> 00:45:37,201
<i>You have six months to live.</i>

659
00:45:37,301 --> 00:45:39,636
Where did you hide
that letter of consent? Answer me!

660
00:45:39,703 --> 00:45:42,039
So, the snake was Director Busujima.

661
00:45:42,106 --> 00:45:43,574
Dr. Daimon, are you fired?

662
00:45:43,640 --> 00:45:45,709
Out of my way. This is my patient.

663
00:45:45,776 --> 00:45:47,444
- Get out now!
- No.
